course: dictionary
lesson: 38
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. A dictionary lists each meaning as a separate numbered sense. «Accept» is a good example: it can mean take something offered, agree that something is true, or say yes to an invitation. The words around it tell you which meaning to choose.
explain: «Never walk off or accept a lift from someone you were not told about.» Here accept means take or agree to go with someone. Ask yourself: what is being accepted? A lift, a gift or an invitation is taken. A fact or an idea is agreed to. The clues in the sentence point to the right meaning.
explain: Accept is a verb, so its ending changes with time: accepts, accepted, accepting. «Old coins can stop being accepted in shops» uses the -ed form for the passive. Try swapping in another word like take or agree. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
fact: Accept means to take what someone offers you, such as a gift or an invitation.
fact: Accept also means to agree that something is true, as in «accept the facts».
fact: To accept someone is to welcome them into a group.
fact: Accepting a mistake and losing gracefully is part of growing up.
exercise: «Never walk off or accept a lift from someone you were not told about.» What does accept mean here? | Ask for a loan of | *Take or agree to go with | Read the name of | Say goodbye to
exercise: Yesterday the shop ___ my old coin. Which word fills the gap? | accept | accepting | *accepted | accepts
exercise: «She accepted the invitation to my party.» What does accepted mean here? | Threw away | *Said yes to | Wrote down | Forgot about
test: «A bet needs both people to agree; nobody owes anything for a deal they never accepted.» What does accepted mean here? | *Agreed to | Lost | Counted | Hidden
test: Accepting differences means what? | Copying your friends | Ignoring people who are not like you | Making people change | *Respecting people who are not like you
exam: Which meaning of accept fits «He would not accept that he had made a mistake»? | To say no to a dare | To welcome into a group | To take a gift | *To agree that it is true
